# Line endings are load-bearing here, not a style preference.
#
# tools/fingerprint.ts hashes the raw bytes of basics/, visualization/build/ and
# each piece's shaders into ref.json, and the sequence exporter's --resume guard
# hashes shader bytes too. Git for Windows checks out CRLF by default, so
# without this file the same commit yields different hashes on Windows than on
# Linux: every reference image would report "basics/ has changed" on a fresh
# clone, and --resume would refuse a directory it had rendered itself, both with
# messages pointing at the wrong thing entirely.
#
# test/layers.test.ts asserts both that this file pins LF and that no source
# file in the tree carries CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Reference and thumbnail images are compared byte for byte. Never touch them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
